    "body": "I very-much agree with having a way to either disable filtering, or allow the list to show all options regardless of the input's value. Assuming that you need an input and not a `<select>`...\nIf the input's value doesn't match anything in the list, then in my opinion it's not intuitive to the user why the list doesn't show when pressing the down-arrow key or focusing/clicking. Similarly, I don't think it's intuitive to new users when the input's value matches a list item, and the list now only shows that matched item, even though the list is doing what it's supposed to. Finally, even if the user is fully knowledgeable with how it works and simply wants to switch to another list item than the one they've typed/chosen, having the list show all options would allow the user to do so with less effort.",
